<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">30 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 30 May, from 1381 to 1989.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1381">1381 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">645 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Peasants' Revolt begins in England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peasants-revolt">Peasants' Revolt</a>, the largest popular rising in medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, broke out, triggered by the third poll tax in four years. Rebels from Essex and Kent marched on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in June, but the rising was put down after Wat Tyler's death.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peasants-revolt">Peasants' Revolt</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1416">1416 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">610 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jerome of Prague is burned for heresy at Constance</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerome">Jerome</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>, a Czech philosopher and theologian and one of the chief followers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-hus">Jan Hus</a>, was burned for heresy at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-constance">Council of Constance</a>. The council had condemned Hus himself, who was burned in 1415.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-constance">Council of Constance</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1431">1431 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">595 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Joan of Arc is burned at the stake in Rouen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Condemned as a relapsed heretic by a church court under English control, Joan died aged about 19. Her conviction was annulled in 1456, and she was canonised in 1920.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1434">1434 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">592 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Utraquists and Catholics defeat the Taborites at Lipany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">East of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>, an alliance of moderate Utraquists and Catholics defeated the radical Taborite and Orphan armies, whose leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prokop-the-great">Prokop the Great</a> was killed. The battle virtually ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussite-wars">Hussite Wars</a> and opened the way to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/compacts-of-basel">Compacts of Basel</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lipany">Battle of Lipany</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussite-wars">Hussite Wars</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/utraquism">Utraquism</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1498">1498 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">528 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Columbus sails on his third voyage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a> left Sanlúcar de Barrameda with six ships. He reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad">Trinidad</a> and the Paria peninsula of Venezuela, his first sight of the South American mainland.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1593">1593 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">433 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Christopher Marlowe is killed in Deptford</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The playwright of Doctor Faustus was stabbed by Ingram Frizer during a dispute over a bill. His links to government espionage have fuelled theories about his death ever since.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1783">1783 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">243 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">America's first daily newspaper appears in Philadelphia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Benjamin Towne's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a> Evening Post began publishing daily, the first newspaper in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> to do so. It folded the following year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1967">1967 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">59 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Biafra declares independence from Nigeria</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Colonel Odumegwu Ojukwu proclaimed the Republic of Biafra in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>'s south-east. The civil war that followed lasted until 1970, and up to two million people died, many from famine.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1989">1989 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Students unveil the Goddess of Democracy in Tiananmen Square</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Art students erected a ten-metre statue facing Mao's portrait as a symbol of the pro-democracy movement. Troops destroyed it when they cleared the square on 4 June.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 30 May <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/theobald-i-of-navarre"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/theobald-i-of-navarre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Theobald I of Navarre</span><span class="tp">1201–1253</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/amadeo-i-of-spain"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amadeo-i-of-spain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Amadeo I of Spain</span><span class="tp">1845–1890</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rene-barrientos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rene-barrientos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">René Barrientos</span><span class="tp">1919–1969</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 30 May <span class="n">10</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/xiao-tong"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/xiao-tong.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Xiao Tong</span><span class="tp">501–531</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-ii-the-exile"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wladyslaw-ii-the-exile.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Władysław II the Exile</span><span class="tp">1105–1159</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/joan-of-arc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Joan of Arc</span><span class="tp">c. 1412–1431</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/prokop-the-great"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/prokop-the-great.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Prokop the Great</span><span class="tp">c. 1380–1434</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/peter-paul-rubens"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/peter-paul-rubens.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Peter Paul Rubens</span><span class="tp">1577–1640</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/voltaire"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/voltaire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Voltaire</span><span class="tp">1694–1778</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ramon-castilla"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ramon-castilla.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ramón Castilla</span><span class="tp">1797–1867</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/prajadhipok"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/prajadhipok.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Prajadhipok</span><span class="tp">1893–1941</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/boris-pasternak"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/boris-pasternak.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Boris Pasternak</span><span class="tp">1890–1960</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rafael-trujillo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rafael-trujillo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Rafael Trujillo</span><span class="tp">1891–1961</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
